Done. Merge `--ff-only 70eea8d1` was already at HEAD. All work is in `v6/labs/prose_nothing/`; `git diff --stat` is empty, no prod code touched.

**What it is:** a dl6 program measuring the "nothing sentence" form (evaluative copula + strawman contrast, minus any receipt token) over `~/.claude/projects/*/*.jsonl`. Hosts only do raw fact extraction (walk transcripts, split sentences, chunk); every regexp, negation, and count is a dl6 rule.

**Artifacts** (`v6/labs/prose_nothing/`): `feed-sentences.mjs` + `feed-sentences.sh` (the sh host), `prose-nothing.dl6` (host, `probe_row`, class rels, `receipt_bearing`, per-side count aggregates), `run.sh` (tsv2 server spin-up copied from `comment-budget-rail.sh`, fixture/corpus modes, idb reads), `fixture-sentences.json`. Report at worktree root: `REPORT-NOTHINGPROSE.md`.

**Results:**

| class | assistant | user | rate/10k (a / u) |
|---|---|---|---|
| sentences | 63,222 | 21,223 | - |
| evaluative_no_receipt | 421 | 146 | 66.59 / 68.79 |
| strawman_contrast | 517 | 50 | 81.78 / 23.56 |
| pure_nothing | 9 | 0 | 1.42 / 0.00 |

Validation: the 6-sentence fixture (one per class, one receipt-bearing evaluative that must not count, one plain sentence) matched its stated expected tallies exactly, verified before the corpus run.

**Key deviations** (full in report §6): the served engine OOMs (macOS SIGKILL) on a single ~20k-row arrival batch, so `run.sh` chunks the corpus to 5,000 rows per probe token with globally disjoint seq ranges. The period/`!`/`?`-only splitter lets `;`/`:`/`and`-joined clauses pair "is right"/"are real" with a contrast phrase in the same extracted sentence, inflating `pure_nothing`; the genuine hits (e.g. the exact flagged sentence, seq 62534) are identifiable in the top-9 list.

Run it: `./v6/labs/prose_nothing/run.sh fixture` and `./v6/labs/prose_nothing/run.sh corpus`.
